,title,link,text,language,family
0,Bantawa language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bantawa_language,"The Bantawa language (also referred to as An Yüng, Bantaba, Bantawa Dum, Bantawa Yong, Bantawa Yüng, Bontawa, Kirawa Yüng) is a Kiranti language spoken in the eastern Himalayan hills of eastern Nepal by Kirati Bantawa ethnic groups. They use a syllabic alphabet system known as Kirat Rai.",Bantawa,Sino-Tibetan
1,Sino-Tibetan languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sino-Tibetan_languages,"Sino-Tibetan (also referred to as Trans-Himalayan) is a family of more than 400 languages, second only to Indo-European in number of native speakers. Around 1.4 billion people speak a Sino-Tibetan language. The vast majority of these are the 1.3 billion native speakers of Sinitic languages.",Bantawa,Sino-Tibetan
2,"Syamunaa Sewaa By Abha Mukarung/Shyam Samsohang Rai - Nepal ...Tibeto-Burman Kiranti language - Bantawa Rai song Paruhang ...Stream Bantawa Sama music | Listen to songs, albums ...Roshan Bantawa Songs, Lyrics & Chords | TunesNepalStream Bantawa music | Listen to songs, albums, playlists for ...Bantawa language and Kirat Rai alphabet - OmniglotBantawa language - Wikipedia",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Te_bBINe-Nk,"Jan 20, 2017 · This video is of Kirat people trying to save their remaining culture and language from extinction. The song is in Bantawa language. Apr 2, 2017 · This is cultural video of Bantawa people during the great Kirat festival of chandi sakela in Nepal. Play Bantawa Sama and discover followers on SoundCloud | Stream tracks, albums, playlists on desktop and mobile. Explore the complete catalog of Roshan Bantawa on TunesNepal. Find chords, lyrics, and music contributions. Play Bantawa and discover followers on SoundCloud | Stream tracks, albums, playlists on desktop and mobile. Bantawa is a member of the Kiranti branch of Sino-Tibetan language family. It is spoken mainly in eastern Nepal, particularly in the Kosi, Mechi and Sagarmatha zones. The Bantawa language (also referred to as An Yüng, Bantaba, Bantawa Dum, Bantawa Yong, Bantawa Yüng, Bontawa, Kirawa Yüng) is a Kiranti language spoken in the eastern Himalayan hills of eastern Nepal by Kirati Bantawa ethnic groups. They use a syllabic alphabet system known as Kirat Rai. Where is Bantawa spoken? Bantawa is a Kiranti language spoken in mainly in Nepal, and also in Bhutan and India, by about 195,100 people. How is Bantawa written? Bantawa is taught in some schools in Nepal and Bhutan, and is used in the media and literature. It is written with a version of the Devanagari alphabet, and used to be written with the Kirat Rai script. Download an alphabet chart for Bantawa (Excel format) Is Bantawa a lingua franca? Bantawa is also considered as a superior clan in the Kiranti family. Bantawa is also reportedly in use as a lingua franca among Rai minorities in Himalayan Sikkim, Darjeeling Kalimpong In India and Bhutan. Meanwhile, the language is just being introduced in a few schools at the primary level (Year 1- Year 5) using Devanagari script. What is Wana Bantawa? Wana Bantawa (also called simply Bantawa), spoken by the Bantawa subcaste. The Amchoke dialect is spoken in the Limbu area, especially in Ilam district. Bantawa is also considered as a superior clan in the Kiranti family.",Bantawa,Sino-Tibetan
